Tome to me.

Tomet is a human-readable, structured markup language and Rust toolchain.
It combines clear syntax for typed data and cross-document links with multi-format export.

==[ Example ]

$raw(tmt("tmtroot/examples/overview.tmt")::source, lang: "tmt")

// @draft| See Also
==[ Try it ]

===[ 1. Install ]

Install `sisho` and `tomet` together using the @link[Quick install](tmt:tmtroot/docs/install_tools.tmt#quick-install):

```bash
`` nix profile install github:tomet-lang/sisho#toolchain
```

===[ 2. Write hello.tmt ]

Create a document `hello.tmt`:

$raw(tmt("tmtroot/examples/hello.tmt")::source, lang: "tmt")

===[ 3. Check it ]

Validate and format your document:

```bash
`` sisho check .
`` sisho fix .
```

Continue with the @link[Quick Start](tmt:tmtroot/docs/quick_start.tmt).

==[ Learn more ]

- @link[Quick Start](tmt:tmtroot/docs/quick_start.tmt): walkthrough for creating, checking, and exporting documents.
- @link[Install](tmt:tmtroot/docs/install_tools.tmt): complete installation instructions for CLI tools and libraries.
- @link[Why Tomet](tmt:tmtroot/docs/why/root.tmt): design motivations and comparison with other formats.
- @link[Specification](tmt:tmtroot/spec/tome.tmt): the language syntax and semantics specification.
- @link[Editors](tmt:tmtroot/docs/install_tools.tmt#editors): extensions and setup for VS Code, Zed, Helix, and Neovim.
- @link[Contributing](tmt:tmtroot/contributing.tmt): guidelines for contributing to Tomet.

==[ Contributing ]

Contributions are welcome.
Repository layout, building from source, running tests, and verification steps are documented in @link[CONTRIBUTING](tmt:tmtroot/contributing.tmt).
